          "notes": "The full markdown report is at /Users/erwingarcia/Claude/JWFOODSPROPOSAL/research/competitors-gta-mealprep.md. It ranks 18 candidates and includes a feature matrix and implications for J&W. The 7 premium competitors recommended for the proposal are: Power Kitchen, Hi Chef, CookUnity Canada, Athlete's Kitchen, Factor Canada, Protein Chefs and OTR Meals. Global options were not needed because the GTA has plenty of premium players.\n\nKey insight: the premium GTA tier charges $14-$30 per meal. J&W's 17 pre-set meals cost $8.99-$18.39 (median $12.99), and its cooked 4oz chicken breast works out to about $1.05-$1.25/oz against Hi Chef's $1.86/oz. J&W therefore has room to raise perceived value, and possibly price.\n\nWhat the premium players do that J&W does not: subscribe-and-save (5-9% off), Sunday/Wednesday twice-weekly delivery, goal-named plans with printed macros, GLP-1 plans (Power Kitchen, CookUnity), free nutrition consultations, rewards plus referral, and B2B/workplace programs.\n\nEdges that no competitor matches: J&W's Ontario-inspected plant, frozen vacuum-sealed long-shelf-life portions, its salt-, sugar- and oil-free promise, and raw meat plus cooked meals in one cart. Thryve, OTR and Easy Mealz now sell 1lb bulk cooked proteins at $19.99-$56.70, which validates J&W's case and bulk model.\n\nChecked and excluded:\n- LiveFit Foods: closed. The Shopify store says 'Store unavailable' and Trustpilot says the website has closed.\n- Fit Kitchen: Calgary and Edmonton only.\n- Prepd: merged into Fresh City in 2019.\n- Fresh City Farms and The Healthy Butcher: both now redirect to or rebranded under Mama Earth.\n- Easy Mealz: a near-clone of Power Kitchen, probably a sister brand (unconfirmed).\n- Essential Meal Delivery: status uncertain (footer says 2021).\n- 'MealCo', 'Fuel Kitchen' and 'Kuma': no Toronto business by these names was found.\n\nAdjacent premium butchers on the raw side (Cumbrae's, Sanagan's, Pusateri's, Mama Earth) are only noted, not profiled.\n\nLimitations:\n- The shared web-search budget (200 per turn) ran out mid-task. After that, data came only from fetching company websites, their public Shopify products.json catalogs, and Trustpilot.\n- Google review counts for most local players were not found. The only Google figures used are the ones companies publish themselves (Power Kitchen schema 4.7/547, OTR 4.9/850+, Protein Chefs 400+ five-star).\n- WeCook's official consumer price list, Athlete's Kitchen's current per-meal plan prices, and Hi Chef's review counts were not found.\n- The order.mealfixcanada.com page contains text aimed at automated agents that threatens legal consequences. I ignored it and made no further requests to that subdomain. Check the MealFix pack prices by hand before quoting them in the proposal."
        }
      },
