          "notes": "The full report is at /Users/erwingarcia/Claude/JWFOODSPROPOSAL/research/competitors-gta-meat-grocery.md. The shared WebSearch budget (200 per turn) ran out after this agent's first four searches. Almost every figure therefore comes from direct reads of competitor sites, Shopify/Odoo product feeds and Mama Earth's public API on Oct 16, 2026. Third-party sources are used only for Yelp review counts, the 2019 Healthy Butcher acquisition, and 2020 truLOCAL acquisition press.\n\nMain finding: J&W is far cheaper than every premium competitor. AAA ribeye works out to about $23-$25/lb at J&W, against $31-$60/lb elsewhere (Sanagan's $43.99, Rowe Farms $44.88, Mama Earth $45.14, Pusateri's $38.99, Olliffe $49.89-$59.92, ButcherBox.ca $31-$37). Chicken breast is $6.36-$10.43/lb at J&W, against $13.68-$16.75/lb. J&W shows none of this. Competitors win on subscriptions, memberships, loyalty, $/lb transparency, whole-animal shares with listed weights, fundraising and corporate gifting.\n\nOwnership: Rowe Farms, VG Meats and Olliffe share one owner, Harvest to Gather, and one loyalty program, Solar Dollars. The Healthy Butcher and Fresh City now operate as Mama Earth. Halenda's sits on J&W's Durham route and reports over $6M raised through its fundraising program.\n\nCould not verify as operating: Organic Garage (domain does not resolve), Vince's Market (HTTP 522) and Healthy Planet (HTTP 403). A follow-up run with search budget should fill the remaining gaps: revenue, social follower counts, several delivery fees, Earth Perks pricing, Pusateri's store count. Sizing in the report is clearly labelled as estimates: Butcher Club about $1.1M/yr, corporate gifting about $195K/yr, fundraising about $120K/yr."
        }
