          "keyTakeaways": [
            "The pool is large and growing slowly. Canada ready meals are CAD 5.0B (2025, ~4% CAGR). That puts the GTA at roughly CAD 0.9B (ESTIMATE, 47% of Ontario at ~39% of Canada).",
            "The weekly-kit model is stalling: 8.5% of Canadians use weekly kits and ~70% of lapsed users quit over cost. Goodfood, Canada's DTC meal leader (41.7% gross margin), saw sales fall 21% in FY2025 and filed for CCAA in Aug 2026. That leaves room for a local, cooked, portioned, high-protein offer from an Ontario-inspected plant.",
            "Online is only ~0-5% of Canadian grocery dollars versus 13% for retail overall, so J&W's Shopify channel has a lot of headroom.",
            "The GTA has ~7.7M people (2025; ~7.6M ESTIMATE for 2026) and ~2.45M households (2021). Toronto alone has 1.16M households, 40% of them non-family, which fits single-portion meal prep.",
            "The fitness audience is large: 15.5% of adults hold gym memberships (~0.9-1.0M GTA adults, ESTIMATE). There are ~2,000 GTA gyms (ESTIMATE), 59 Ontario CrossFit boxes, and ~31,460 fitness instructors/trainers in the Toronto region, 31% self-employed. That is a ready affiliate channel for the 'EAT CLEAN - TRAIN MEAN' brand.",
            "Retention is the economic swing factor. Meal kits churn 8-15% a month (M12 retention 15-28%), while replenishment-style standing orders keep 40-55% at 12 months. J&W should sell a skip/pause 'standing order', not a kit.",
            "Paid acquisition benchmarks for food DTC: Meta CPA US$38.57 (~C$55) and Google CPA US$23.65 (~C$34). Use an ESTIMATE of C$60-120 for new-customer CAC in a GTA-only campaign.",
            "Owned channels are cheap: Klaviyo flows produce ~41% of email revenue from 5.3% of sends, and food & beverage SMS flows earn US$1.83 per recipient. Reviews raise purchase likelihood 270% at 5 reviews, and J&W has zero reviews on 979 products.",
            "About $1M a year is C$19.2k a week. Plausible single routes: ~320 biweekly C$120 subscribers, 50 partner gyms at C$400/week, ~115 corporate gifting clients x 60 boxes x C$120, 25-60 smart fridges, or 60 youth sports teams in season (all ESTIMATES).",
            "Margin mix matters: cooked meal prep (~40-50% ESTIMATE, Goodfood benchmark 41.7%) is worth about 1.5-2x raw meat (~25-35% ESTIMATE; US grocery 26%, food processing 23%). Marketplaces take 20-30% (Uber Eats 20/25/30%, DoorDash 20/25/29%), so list only cooked meals there.",
            "Delivery cost inputs: Ontario minimum wage is $17.95 (Oct 2026), the Toronto driver median is $21/h, and a new reefer van costs ~C$100-135k (converted from US listings). ESTIMATE owned-route cost of C$8-14 per stop, which J&W's $20 route fee on a $100 minimum already covers.",
            "Gaps: cold-chain courier rate cards, butcher-shop margins, Ontario Soccer counts, Instacart merchant fees and a current Canadian per-employee corporate gifting figure were not found (the workflow's web-search budget ran out partway through). They are labelled as estimates in /Users/erwingarcia/Claude/JWFOODSPROPOSAL/research/market-benchmarks.md."
          ]
        }
