        "correctedClaims": [
          "Acquisition 'reported at about C$16.8M': EMERGE's own release says 'up to $16.8M'. That is a ceiling including earn-outs: $6.5M cash + 4,666,667 shares upfront, $1.5M deferred, and up to $4.5M earn-out. truLOCAL's revenue was about $19.8M in 2020.",
          "'Every box carries a FREE Meat for Life item': the item goes only to NEW customers who activate one promo (one choice of steak, chicken, salmon or ground beef), for as long as the subscription stays active. It cannot be combined with other offers, and the 10-year version caps at 120 boxes.",
          "'Tiered discounts for 10-1,000 gifts': as fetched on Oct 16 2026, the gifts page publishes no discount tiers or percentages and no 1,000 figure. The quote form uses quantity bands (<10, 11-25, 26-50, 51-100, 100+) and there is no minimum.",
          "'Sells 100% grass-fed and finished beef, organic chicken': these are lines, not the whole range. The catalog also lists AAA/AA+ graded beef and RWA (non-organic) chicken, and there is no Wagyu.",
          "'Warehouses in Ontario, Alberta and BC': the site says only that it 'operates out of' ON, AB and BC and publishes no warehouse addresses. The 2021 release listed a Kitchener HQ plus Vancouver, Calgary and Chicago offices/facilities.",
          "Wild Fork: FOUR Ontario stores close by Dec 14 2026 (Whitby, Oakville, Ancaster, Newmarket), not three. Ancaster is in Hamilton, which is on J&W's Thursday GTA 3 route.",
          "'400 subscribers ≈ 0.6% of truLOCAL's 70,100-customer base': 70,100 is cumulative customers served since 2016, not active subscribers. The active count is not disclosed.",
          "'J&W can undercut truLOCAL's tiers': per serving the proposed tiers barely undercut. Starter $129/~30 servings is $4.30 vs truLOCAL's $4.31; Family $229/70 is $3.27 vs $3.49; Freezer Fill $299/95 is $3.15 vs $3.36. With J&W's $20 route fee, J&W is at or above truLOCAL at every tier.",
          "Revenue lever 'x 11-12 boxes': truLOCAL's own CLTV (about $2,000) / AOV (about $240) implies roughly 8 lifetime orders per customer. Model churn: holding 250-400 active members needs about 375-600 new members a year (ESTIMATE). truLOCAL's AOV of about $240 does support J&W's $159-229 average-box assumption as conservative."
        ]
