      {
        "name": "Calo (calo.app): Riyadh-based healthy meal-plan subscriptions across KSA, UAE, Kuwait, Qatar, Bahrain, Oman and the UK (Detox Kitchen and Fresh Fitness Food were folded into Calo UK)",
        "verifiedOperating": true,
        "verificationNote": "Calo is operating and premium as of Oct 16, 2026. Evidence:\n- The menu page shows this week's menu, dated 11–17 Oct.\n- The latest blog post is dated Oct 7, 2026, and the footer reads © 2026 Calo Inc.\n- The plans-page config contains a \"pricingKSAMay2026Control\" pricing test and a Ramadan 2026 feature flag.\n\nUK is live under the Calo brand:\n- Detox Kitchen's site says it is now Calo: Calo launched as a standalone UK brand on 1 March (no year stated), and DK meals became Calo-branded from 28 April.\n- Calo published UK posts in April 2026 (Calo vs COOK / Simmer Eats / Prep Kitchen, London Marathon).\n- CB Insights dates the Fresh Fitness Food acquisition to Apr 24, 2025, and freshfitnessfood.com no longer resolves.\n\nCalo has no Canadian or North American presence. The country selector lists only the GCC countries plus UK and World.\n\nLimits: the web-search budget was used up, so news is limited to Wamda and CB Insights. calo.app/en-gb redirects from Canada to the global /en page, so UK facts come from Calo's blog and detoxkitchen.co.uk. Notes are in /Users/erwingarcia/Claude/JWFOODSPROPOSAL/research/competitor-06.md.",
        "premiumEvidence": "Funding and growth (Wamda, 29 Jul 2025):\n- US$64M Series B: US$25M in Dec 2024 led by Nuwa Capital, plus a US$39M extension in Jul 2025 led by AlJazira Capital, oversubscribed beyond a US$50M target.\n- 50%+ year-on-year growth in H1 2025, and 10M+ meals in 2024.\n- \"Nine-figure\" annualised revenue is claimed but no figure was ever published: the release contains an unfilled \"($ million)\" placeholder.\n- Saudi IPO planned. Premium-gym partner Armah Sports, whose founder sits on Calo's board.\n\nCompany claims on its own pages:\n- 280K GCC customers and 18M meals on the KSA page; 290K and 19M on the newer global page.\n- 95+ meals a week; 25+ new meals a month.\n- 12 café locations (Wamda said 10+ in Jul 2025), including Kingdom Hospital and employee-only cafés inside SNB, Zakat Authority and Roshn.\n- 100+ corporate catering clients, with logos for Surface, Alinma Bank, STC and NBB.\n- HACCP and ISO 22000:2018 kitchens.\n- 24/7 support with a stated 90-second average response.\n\nPremium bundles and pricing:\n- Calo Pro annual bundle: 12-month gym membership, a WHOOP tracker and a smart-scale kit.\n- Custom Macros is priced about 32–37% above standard plans.\n\nAI: \"Calo Black\", an LLM private chef, was announced as a pilot in Jul 2025. No public product was found on calo.app in Oct 2026.",
        "pricing": "KSA prices, taken from the plans-page config and shown here including 15% VAT. CAD conversions are approximate, at 1 SAR ≈ C$0.379 (SAR pegged at 3.75/USD; BoC 1.4196 CAD/USD on Oct 15, 2026).\n\nPer meal:\n- Balanced/Vegetarian: lunch or dinner SAR 36 (≈C$13.65), breakfast SAR 26, snack SAR 12.\n- High Protein/Low Carb: lunch or dinner SAR 36, breakfast SAR 30, snack SAR 18.\n- Custom Macros: lunch or dinner SAR 47.50 (≈C$18, +32% vs Balanced), breakfast SAR 37.50, snack SAR 18.\n- The home page's \"from SAR 31/meal, SAR 23/breakfast\" is the price before VAT.\n\nPer day, monthly or quarterly cycle:\n- Lunch + snack (the minimum): SAR 50 (≈C$19) Balanced, SAR 56 High Protein, SAR 67.50 Custom Macros.\n- Full day (breakfast, lunch, dinner, snack): SAR 110 (≈C$41.70) Balanced, SAR 120 High Protein, SAR 150.50 (≈C$57) Custom Macros.\n- Skip-breakfast and skip-dinner presets run SAR 74–113.\n- The weekly cycle costs SAR 12/day more, and the config lists a SAR 10 weekly delivery charge (unit not stated). Monthly and quarterly delivery is free.\n\nRules and payment:\n- Minimum of 2 meals a day, including lunch or dinner, and 5 days a week.\n- Auto-renew is on by default for monthly and weekly plans, off for quarterly.\n- Payment by card, Apple Pay or mada, or buy-now-pay-later through Tabby or Tamara (pay in 4; Tamara minimum SAR 390). Promo code TRY15 gives 15% off.\n\nBundles:\n- 1x1: a monthly plan plus a 1-month gym membership.\n- 3x3: a quarterly plan plus 3 months at Fitness Time.\n- Calo Pro: annual only, \"worth 8,000\" (currency not stated), up to 12 instalments; the price did not render.\n\nUK:\n- £9–£10 per meal, with free daily delivery nationwide except Northern Ireland and the Highlands (Calo blog, Apr 20, 2026).\n- The Detox Kitchen rebrand cut its prices by about 30%.\n\nSanity check for J&W's planned C$180/week Personal Macro Plan (ESTIMATE): Calo Custom Macros costs ≈C$128/week for lunch + snack over 5 days, and ≈C$285/week for a full day over 5 days. C$180 sits inside that range.",
        "scale": "- **Funding:** US$64M Series B (2024–25).\n- **Revenue:** \"nine-figure\" US$ annualised, but no figure was published. Growth was 50%+ year on year in H1 2025.\n- **Customers and meals:** 290K customers and 19M meals delivered (company claim on the global page; the KSA page says 280K / 18M). 10M+ meals in 2024.\n- **Markets:** 6 GCC countries plus the UK, with 25+ KSA cities served from Riyadh and Jeddah kitchens.\n- **Physical sites:** 12 cafés.\n- **Corporate:** 100+ catering clients.\n- **Menu:** 95+ meals a week (UK: 100+ new meals a week).\n- **Not found:** app-store rating and Trustpilot score. Calo is not present in Canada.",
        "siteDesign": "Built on Next.js with full English/Arabic (right-to-left) support.\n\nPalette (read from Calo's CSS):\n- Primary green #24A170, used for pill CTAs and icons.\n- Dark greens #28864C, #1C7E57, #166144 and deepest #114B34; bright greens #3CAD68 and #28B17B.\n- Mint tints #EAF7F2, #EDF5F0, #BCE7D6, #98D9B1, #8ED2B7, used as testimonial and section backgrounds.\n- Text charcoal #343B42; secondary text #697886.\n- Borders #EBEDEF and #DDE0E4; disabled #BDC4CB; light panels #F9FAFB and #F5F6F7.\n- Macro accent dots: protein purple #987DDE, carbs amber #F4B248, fat blue #64ACEC. Error red #E35044.\n\nTypography:\n- A self-hosted humanist sans that renders like Lato. H1 is 64/72px at weight 900 in charcoal; body is 16px; buttons are 14px bold.\n- Bebas Neue (condensed, all caps) is the display face for a kinetic statement band.\n- The logo is a spaced, all-caps green wordmark.\n- Shapes: pill buttons (999px radius); soft borderless cards at 12–20px radius, large panels at 32px.\n\nLayout, top to bottom:\n1. A split 50/50 hero. The left half is white, with an H1 that cycles through audiences (busy people, lose weight, gain muscle, high performers), one pill CTA, and a small green stats line at the bottom. The right half is a full-bleed lifestyle photo.\n2. A centred \"daily-changing menu\" section with 3 trust icons. Dish cards scroll sideways, each with a kcal chip, the dish name and coloured macro dots, with diet filter pills below.\n3. A control/flexibility section: accordion tabs on the left, autoplay video on the right.\n4. Three numbered steps with dark-green badges.\n5. A green band with Bebas Neue kinetic text.\n6. Testimonial cards on mint.\n7. A plan carousel with overhead food photos and macro-split chips.\n8. An FAQ accordion of grey rows, beside a mint \"chat with us\" card with support-agent avatars.\n9. A creator (UGC) carousel.\n10. A footer with an app QR code and a country/language switcher.\n\nPlans page: a two-column configurator with a sticky live price card on the right.\n\nPhotography:\n- Overhead plated meals on white plates against light stone, in soft natural light.\n- Lifestyle shots of diverse people eating from branded bowls in warm interiors (deep green walls, wood), with the branded tote and cup visible.\n\nTone: short, punchy, second person, lightly witty. It uses two-beat headline pairs and question-then-answer bands. It promises outcomes (macros hit, no prep), sells flexibility, and stresses no contracts.",
        "keyFlows": [
          "PLAN CONFIGURATOR (/plans-and-packages). Two columns with a sticky summary card. (1) Pick a diet from 5 emoji cards: Balanced, Custom Macros, Low-Carb, High Protein, Vegetarian; each has 'View menu' and 'Select Plan', and Custom Macros uses 'Build my plan'. (2) Choose meals per day from chips: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Snack; minimum 2, including lunch or dinner. (3) Pick days from an S-M-T-W-T-F-S row of circle toggles; minimum 5. (4) Choose a payment cycle (Weekly, Monthly or 3-months), with optional gym logos; buy-now-pay-later in 4 instalments on monthly and 3-month plans. (5) The summary card ('Your package awaits, from 50/Day') updates live; press Continue. (6) Create an account with a phone number (+966). (7) Pay by card, Apple Pay, mada, Tabby or Tamara.",
          "CUSTOM MACROS CALCULATOR. A modal stepper; step names are taken from the site's JavaScript. Steps: birthday, then gender (2 emoji cards), height in cm (50-300), weight, activity level (4 emoji cards: sedentary, lightly active, very active, highly active), goal (lose weight, gain weight, build muscle, maintain), target, calories (pre-calculated, searchable dropdown in 5-kcal steps), protein, carbs. The result is a stacked macro bar with an 'Edit macros' link, and the plan is then selected. Analytics events fire at start, calculated, edited and plan-selected, so drop-off is measured at each stage.",
          "SUBSCRIPTION SELF-SERVICE IN THE APP. Customers can edit the menu, swap any item, skip, pause, or change address or time slot. The cutoff is 48 hours in the GCC and 24 hours (1 business day) in the UK. To pause: Account Settings, then Pause Subscription, then pick a duration. Customers can exclude any number of ingredients per meal and build their own meal if nothing on the menu suits. The app saves favourites, dislikes and allergies and offers AI macro tracking and progress tracking. There are no contracts; monthly plans auto-renew by default.",
          "PRESET MEAL COMBINATIONS. Preset packages per day: 'Business Lunch' (lunch + snack), 'Skip Breakfast', 'Skip Dinner', 'Full', plus seasonal Ramadan and Futoor (Iftar) presets. Each preset is multiplied by the diet type and payment cycle to give a price per day.",
          "CORPORATE CATERING CHECKOUT, NO QUOTES. (1) Pick dishes, serving sizes and quantities from a 100+ dish menu with calories shown and nut-free, gluten-free and dairy-free filters. (2) Pay by card or buy-now-pay-later. (3) Delivered within 48 hours. (4) Serve. Every call to action reads 'Place Your Order', and client logos sit alongside a '100+ businesses' stat.",
          "COACH AND CREATOR AFFILIATE PROGRAM. (1) Fill in a 30-second form. (2) A review takes 15-30 days, after which approved partners get an account manager. (3) The partner receives a personal discount code, and their client gets a first-order discount. (4) The partner earns tokens each time the code is used. Referral, wallet and cashback pages exist on the site.",
          "NUTRITIONIST CALL. 'Book a call' for a 15-20 minute session with a nutritionist to work out calories and choose a plan, or a 10-minute general call about pricing and delivery. Call details are sent on confirmation.",
          "GYM BUNDLES AND ANNUAL 'PRO' TIER. 1x1: a monthly plan plus 1 month of gym membership. 3x3: a quarterly plan plus 3 months at Fitness Time. Calo Pro is annual only and bundles a 12-month gym membership, a WHOOP tracker and a smart-scale kit, payable in 12 instalments, with pauses of up to 60 days.",
          "MARKET ADD-ONS AND CAFE. Subscribers can add snacks, frozen items and supplements from Calo Market to their meal delivery for free. The cafe is ordered in the app (Cafe, then menu, then order) and collected at the counter or by Car Hop, with 30% off the first order. Some cafes are employee-only sites inside corporations, and one is inside a hospital."
        ],
        "featuresToBorrow": [
          "A rotating-audience hero ('Meal Butler for ... lean gains / fat loss / busy families / GLP-1'), with a stats line (4.8 stars from 611 Google reviews, years in business) and one green pill CTA.",
          "Dish cards with a kcal chip and coloured protein, carb and fat dots, plus diet filter pills. This also fixes J&W's 51% empty descriptions, because AI can write the copy and macros from the weighed portions.",
          "A plan configurator with a sticky live 'from $X/day' summary. Steps: goal, then meals per day, then days, then cycle. Presets like 'Lunch + Snack', 'Skip Breakfast' and 'Full Day', all built from existing Meal Butler SKUs.",
          "A Custom Macros wizard (birthday, sex, height, weight, activity, goal, then calories with editable protein and carbs) that feeds an AI-built weekly cart. Charge a premium tier at about +30%, which matches Calo's +32% custom-macro premium.",
          "A lower price per day for a monthly commitment than for week-to-week (Calo charges about SAR 12/day more for weekly), with auto-renew on by default and buy-now-pay-later on large packages.",
          "Self-serve skip, pause, swap and exclusions up to a cutoff, which for J&W is the Sunday order deadline. Use Shopify subscription or customer-portal apps.",
          "Gym bundles and an annual 'Pro' tier: a GTA gym partner membership, an InBody scan every 4 weeks, and a smart scale or tracker, payable in instalments.",
          "A coach and trainer affiliate program with personal codes, a first-order discount for clients and rewards per use. This targets the 8-12K independent GTA trainers.",
          "Self-serve corporate catering and 'Large Orders' checkout with no quote step and delivery within 48 hours, plus client logos.",
          "A free 15-20 minute nutrition call as the first-subscription hook, staffed by Lucas, Tasia or a partner dietitian.",
          "Grocery and snack add-ons to a standing order. J&W's 600+ grocery, Greek and supplement SKUs become cart add-ons, the way Calo Market items join the meal delivery.",
          "Comparison SEO posts ('J&W vs Power Kitchen', 'vs Factor'), which Calo runs for the UK market.",
          "An FAQ accordion beside a live-chat card with real staff faces, and a creator UGC carousel that draws on J&W's 30K Instagram followers."
        ],
        "whatJWDoesBetter": [
          "Its own Ontario-inspected meat plant (since 2008) and a family butcher and wholesale lineage in Toronto going back to the early 1960s and 1973; J&W itself dates from 1995. Calo is a tech-led meal-plan start-up founded in 2019, with no butchery.",
          "Raw and cooked food in one cart: 979 SKUs, including AAA, Canadian Prime and Wagyu beef, quarter cows, whole lambs and gift boxes. Calo sells only prepared meals and snacks.",
          "True a-la-carte cooked portions by the ounce (4, 5, 6 and 8 oz proteins, egg bites, oats, sides) with no plan minimum. Calo requires at least 2 meals a day, 5 days a week, starting at SAR 50/day.",
          "Everything is salt-free and sugar-free with no added oils. Calo cooks mainly with extra-virgin olive oil and uses butter or coconut oil in some desserts.",
          "Price (ESTIMATE): a J&W day built from the catalogue costs about C$28.55-32.55 (egg bites + oats; Greek Lemon chicken + basmati + broccoli; a pre-set dinner). Calo's full day costs about C$41.70 on Balanced and about C$57 on Custom Macros, so J&W is roughly 25-50% cheaper.",
          "Flash-frozen, vacuum-sealed portions on one weekly route across a wide part of Ontario. Calo's model needs costly daily fresh delivery.",
          "Ontario-raised, air-chilled, grain-fed chicken with no hormones or antibiotics.",
          "A local human brand: Brimley Rd store with free pickup, owners customers know by name (Bill, Tasia, Lucas), and 4.8 stars from 611 Google reviews.",
          "No local Calo: Calo is absent from Canada, so the premium personalised tier in the GTA is open."
        ],
        "correctedClaims": [
          "Revenue: 'high-growth nine-figure annualised revenue' is a company claim with no number. The Wamda press text contains an unfilled '($ million)' placeholder.",
          "Customer and meal counts: 280K GCC customers and 18M meals is the KSA page. The global page now shows 290K customers and 19M meals.",
          "Edit cutoff: 'Pause, skip or edit up to 48h before delivery' is the GCC rule. In the UK the cutoff is 24 hours (1 business day).",
          "Calo Black was announced as a pilot in July 2025. No public Calo Black product or mention was found on calo.app in October 2026. Treat it as an unconfirmed pilot.",
          "'Customer's name on each label (the Fresh Fitness Food model)' cannot be verified now: freshfitnessfood.com no longer resolves, and Calo UK pages do not mention name labels. Present it as J&W's own idea.",
          "Physical sites: the cafe page now lists 12 locations, compared with '10+' in Wamda (Jul 2025).",
          "The UK runs under the Calo brand. Calo launched as a standalone UK brand on 1 March (no year given) and Detox Kitchen meals became Calo-branded from 28 April. CB Insights dates the Fresh Fitness Food acquisition to Apr 24, 2025."
        ],
        "sources": [
